      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the child as the speaker of the text",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the child, who is visually depicted as the speaker of the text 'my dad is the best at hide and seek'. The child's solemn expression and the context of the text imply that the child is the one who is speaking these words, even though the text is presented as a statement about the child's experience. The visual material (the child) is mapped onto the textual material (the statement) as the entity being referred to by the text. The user sees themselves in the child's perspective, projecting their own experience or empathy onto the child as the speaker.",
